    "introduction": [
      "A generator set converts fuel into electrical power on site: an engine drives an alternator, a controller starts, loads and protects the pair, and the support subsystems — fuel, cooling, lubrication, starting and exhaust aftertreatment — keep the engine able to run. Several sets may be paralleled onto one bus, and a transfer switch decides whether a load is fed from the utility or from the set.",
      "Every one of those parts already reports data. The engine speaks SAE J1939 over a CAN bus, the controller exposes its own protocol, the transfer switch another. What is missing is a common description: an integrator wanting engine load, alternator power and the operating state of a set has to learn one vendor's map, then the next vendor's, and again for every fleet.",
      "This document defines that common description as an OPC UA information model. It gives a generator set, its components, its ratings, its operating state machine and its protections a standard type, so that a Client reads the same BrowseNames, DataTypes and engineering units whatever equipment is behind them."
    ],
    "draftBanner": "PROVISIONAL WORKING DRAFT — not normative, not endorsed by the OPC Foundation. The document number, the Mantis project identifier and every NodeId in this document are placeholders; the OPC Foundation assigns the real values."
  },

